---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const image = base + '/images/australia-night-oceans.webp';
const atlasPreview = base + '/images/sky-atlas-preview.png';
const atlasTiles = base + '/tiles/sky-atlas/{z}/{x}/{y}.webp';
const parkBoundariesUrl = base + '/data/selected-national-parks.geojson';
const roadsUrl = base + '/data/major-roads.geojson';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-AU">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Explore Australia's modelled artificial sky brightness in an interactive adaptation of the Dark Sky QGIS project." />
    <link rel="icon" href={base + '/favicon.svg'} />
    <title>Australia After Dark | GIS Carto Sandbox</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <header><a href={base + '/'}>Portfolio</a></header>
      <section class="intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">AUSTRALIA · DARK SKIES</p>
        <h1>Where the stars still win</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Australia after dark</p>
        <p>Explore a model of Australia's artificial sky brightness, then compare it with satellite night lights. Choose a place to begin, or pan and zoom freely.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="guide" aria-labelledby="guide-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">GUIDED VIEWS</p><h2 id="guide-title">Follow the dark</h2></div><p>Six places, from the national pattern to individual parks.</p></div>
        <div class="stop-grid">
          <button class="stop" data-stop="australia" aria-pressed="true"><small>01 · NATIONAL</small><strong>Australia</strong><span>Coast and interior</span></button>
          <button class="stop" data-stop="seq" aria-pressed="false"><small>02 · REGIONAL</small><strong>South East Queensland</strong><span>City halo and hinterland</span></button>
          <button class="stop" data-stop="watarrka" aria-pressed="false"><small>03 · PARK</small><strong>Watarrka</strong><span>Central Australia</span></button>
          <button class="stop" data-stop="carnarvon" aria-pressed="false"><small>04 · PARK</small><strong>Carnarvon Gorge</strong><span>Central Queensland</span></button>
          <button class="stop" data-stop="girraween" aria-pressed="false"><small>05 · PARK</small><strong>Girraween</strong><span>Granite Belt</span></button>
          <button class="stop" data-stop="munga" aria-pressed="false"><small>06 · PARK</small><strong>Munga-Thirri</strong><span>Channel Country</span></button>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="map-panel" aria-label="Interactive map of Australian night lights">
        <div class="toolbar">
          <div class="legend" aria-label="Map symbols">
            <span><i class="city"></i> Capital city</span>
            <span><i class="town"></i> Regional centre</span>
            <span><i class="park"></i> National park</span>
            <span><i class="park-boundary"></i> Park boundary</span>
            <span><i class="road"></i> Major road</span>
          </div>
          <div class="map-actions"><div class="mode-switch" aria-label="Imagery layer"><button type="button" data-mode="atlas" aria-pressed="true">Sky brightness</button><button type="button" data-mode="satellite" aria-pressed="false">Satellite lights</button></div>
          <button id="reset-extent" type="button" disabled>Reset</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="layer-options"><span>SHOW ON MAP</span><label title="Hillshade appears when you zoom in to regional scale"><input id="show-relief" type="checkbox" /> Terrain relief</label><label class="relief-strength" for="relief-strength">Strength <input id="relief-strength" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="50" disabled /><output id="relief-value" for="relief-strength">50%</output></label><label><input id="show-parks" type="checkbox" checked /> Park outlines</label><label><input id="show-roads" type="checkbox" checked /> Major roads</label><span class="map-hint">Drag to pan · scroll, pinch, or use + and − to zoom</span></div>
        <div id="night-map" data-image={image} data-atlas={atlasTiles} data-parks={parkBoundariesUrl} data-roads={roadsUrl} aria-label="Modelled artificial sky brightness across Australia with selected park boundaries and major roads. Drag to pan or use the zoom buttons.">
          <img class="fallback" src={atlasPreview} alt="Coloured map of modelled artificial sky brightness across Australia" />
        </div>
        <div class="map-caption"><p class="caption" id="map-scale" role="status">National view</p><p class="source-note">Modelled sky brightness · 2016 atlas</p></div>
        <div class="sky-key" aria-label="Artificial sky brightness from darkest to brightest"><strong>ARTIFICIAL SKY BRIGHTNESS</strong><div class="swatches"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="key-ends"><span>Near-natural</span><span>Brightest</span></div></div>
      </section>
      <section class="view-note" aria-live="polite"><p class="eyebrow">IN VIEW</p><h2 id="view-title">Australia</h2><p id="view-description">The national view shows the broad contrast between concentrated light around population centres and the darker interior.</p></section>
      <section class="nearby" aria-labelledby="nearby-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM BRISBANE</p><h2 id="nearby-title">A darker night, closer to home</h2></div><p>Three park areas to explore within roughly four hours' drive. Times are indicative, and the atlas is a historical model rather than a forecast.</p></div>
        <div class="near-grid">
          <article><span class="travel-time">ABOUT 3 HOURS</span><h3>Bunya Mountains</h3><p>Compare the park's modelled sky with the brighter centres of the Darling Downs and South Burnett.</p><button class="text-link" data-stop="bunya">View on map →</button><a href="https://parks.qld.gov.au/parks/bunya-mountains" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Park information ↗</a></article>
          <article><span class="travel-time">ABOUT 3½ HOURS</span><h3>Girraween</h3><p>Look beyond the Granite Belt towns to see how the coloured bands change around the park.</p><button class="text-link" data-stop="girraween">View on map →</button><a href="https://parks.qld.gov.au/parks/girraween" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Park information ↗</a></article>
          <article><span class="travel-time">ABOUT 3–4 HOURS</span><h3>Sundown</h3><p>The atlas shows a dark area around this border country park; use the map to compare it with nearby towns.</p><button class="text-link" data-stop="sundown">View on map →</button><a href="https://parks.qld.gov.au/parks/sundown" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Park information ↗</a></article>
        </div>
        <p class="travel-note">Drive times are approximate figures published by Queensland Parks. Check the specific access point, road conditions, park rules, moon and weather before planning a night visit.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="notes">
        <h2>Reading the map</h2>
        <p>The default map uses my original QGIS Dark Sky project: modelled artificial zenith sky brightness from the 2016 World Atlas. The source raster is about 1 km per pixel, served here as local tiles so it stays detailed while panning and zooming. Black represents near-natural modelled skies. At closer scales, selected park boundaries and a generalised major road network provide context. Optional terrain relief adds topographic shape; it does not change the sky brightness values. Park markers indicate approximate locations; the Carnarvon Gorge marker sits within the larger Carnarvon National Park. This historical model does not describe current viewing conditions.</p>
        <p>Sky brightness data: <a href="https://doi.org/10.5880/GFZ.1.4.2016.001">Falchi et al. (2016), New World Atlas of Artificial Night Sky Brightness</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/">CC BY-NC 4.0</a>. Terrain relief: <a href="https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md">Mapzen Elevation</a>. Park boundaries: <a href="https://www.dcceew.gov.au/environment/land/nrs/science/capad">CAPAD 2024</a>, Commonwealth of Australia. Roads: <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/downloads/10m-cultural-vectors/roads/">Natural Earth 1:10m</a>, public domain. Satellite option: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/earth-at-night/maps/">NASA Black Marble 2016</a> via NASA GIBS. Map built with <a href="https://leafletjs.com/">Leaflet</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script>
      import L from 'leaflet';
      import 'leaflet/dist/leaflet.css';
      import 'leaflet-relief';
      import { capitals, centres, parks, type Place } from '../../data/australia-after-dark';

      const container = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#night-map')!;
      const reset = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#reset-extent')!;
      const modeButtons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-mode]');
      const roadsToggle = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#show-roads')!;
      const parksToggle = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#show-parks')!;
      const reliefToggle = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#show-relief')!;
      const reliefStrength = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#relief-strength')!;
      const reliefValue = document.querySelector<HTMLOutputElement>('#relief-value')!;
      const viewTitle = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#view-title')!;
      const viewDescription = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#view-description')!;
      const sourceNote = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.source-note')!;
      const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#map-scale')!;
      const projection = L.CRS.EPSG3857;
      const rasterBounds = L.latLngBounds(
        projection.unproject(L.point(9500000, -6500000)),
        projection.unproject(L.point(19000000, -450000)),
      );
      const australia = L.latLngBounds([-49, 100], [-7, 165]);
      const map = L.map(container, {
        minZoom: 2, maxZoom: 8, zoomSnap: 0.25,
        maxBounds: rasterBounds.pad(0.55), maxBoundsViscosity: 0.75,
        scrollWheelZoom: true,
        wheelPxPerZoomLevel: 40,
        wheelDebounceTime: 20,
        touchZoom: true,
      });
      const stops: Record<string, { title: string; description: string; bounds: [[number, number], [number, number]] }> = {
        australia: { title: 'Australia', description: 'The national view shows the broad contrast between concentrated light around population centres and the darker interior.', bounds: [[-49, 100], [-7, 165]] },
        seq: { title: 'South East Queensland', description: 'Follow the Brisbane–Gold Coast light halo, then compare it with the inland towns and nearby national parks.', bounds: [[-29.7, 150.3], [-25.5, 154.2]] },
        watarrka: { title: 'Watarrka', description: 'Look at the Watarrka National Park boundary in Central Australia and the modelled sky brightness around it.', bounds: [[-24.8, 130.6], [-23.7, 132.5]] },
        carnarvon: { title: 'Carnarvon Gorge', description: 'The gorge marker lies within the larger Carnarvon National Park. Compare its outline with the nearby pools of artificial sky brightness.', bounds: [[-25.8, 147.3], [-24.4, 149.1]] },
        girraween: { title: 'Girraween', description: 'Explore the Granite Belt park and compare its modelled sky with Stanthorpe and the surrounding towns.', bounds: [[-29.25, 151.3], [-28.4, 152.5]] },
        munga: { title: 'Munga-Thirri', description: 'Explore a broad remote park landscape in western Queensland and the sparse light signatures around it.', bounds: [[-27.4, 136.5], [-24.0, 140.0]] },
        bunya: { title: 'Bunya Mountains', description: 'Compare the park with the modelled sky brightness around the Darling Downs and South Burnett.', bounds: [[-27.3, 150.9], [-26.2, 152.4]] },
        sundown: { title: 'Sundown', description: 'The atlas depicts dark modelled skies in the park area, southwest of the brighter Granite Belt towns.', bounds: [[-29.2, 151.2], [-28.4, 152.3]] },
      };
      const resetView = () => map.fitBounds(australia, { padding: [18, 18], animate: false });
      resetView();
      reset.disabled = false;
      function selectStop(id: string) {
        const stop = stops[id];
        if (!stop) return;
        viewTitle.textContent = stop.title;
        viewDescription.textContent = stop.description;
        document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.stop').forEach(button => button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(button.dataset.stop === id)));
        map.flyToBounds(stop.bounds, { padding: [24, 24], maxZoom: 7.75, duration: 0.8 });
        if (document.querySelector('.nearby button[data-stop="' + id + '"]')) container.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      }
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-stop]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => selectStop(button.dataset.stop!)));
      reset.addEventListener('click', () => selectStop('australia'));
      L.control.scale({ imperial: false }).addTo(map);
      const satelliteOverview = L.imageOverlay(container.dataset.image!, rasterBounds).on('load', () => {
        container.classList.add('has-map');
      }).on('error', () => {
        status.textContent = 'Satellite imagery could not be loaded.';
      });

      const skyAtlas = L.tileLayer(container.dataset.atlas!, {
        minZoom: 3, maxNativeZoom: 8, maxZoom: 8,
        bounds: L.latLngBounds([-44.8, 112.9], [-9.2, 159.2]), noWrap: true,
        attribution: 'Falchi et al. 2016 · CC BY-NC 4.0',
      }).on('load', () => container.classList.add('has-map')).addTo(map);

      const reliefPane = map.createPane('terrain-relief');
      reliefPane.style.zIndex = '300';
      reliefPane.style.pointerEvents = 'none';
      reliefPane.style.mixBlendMode = 'screen';
      const terrainRelief = L.gridLayer.relief({
        pane: 'terrain-relief', mode: 'hillshade', minZoom: 5, maxZoom: 8,
        elevationUrl: L.GridLayer.Relief.elevationUrls.terrarium,
        attribution: L.GridLayer.Relief.elevationAttributions.terrarium,
        opacity: 0.38, hillshadeExaggeration: 1.1,
        // Black has no effect with screen blending; only lit slopes add a faint highlight.
        hillshadeColorFunction: intensity => {
          const highlight = Math.round(Math.max(0, intensity - 0.62) * 150);
          return [highlight, highlight, highlight];
        },
      });

      const detailPane = map.createPane('night-detail');
      detailPane.style.zIndex = '350';
      detailPane.style.pointerEvents = 'none';
      // Use native tiles at regional scales. The local overview stays underneath
      // so a failed or slow tile request never leaves a blank patch.
      const nightDetail = L.tileLayer(
        'https://gibs.earthdata.nasa.gov/wmts/epsg3857/best/VIIRS_Black_Marble/default/2016-01-01/GoogleMapsCompatible_Level8/{z}/{y}/{x}.png',
        { pane: 'night-detail', minZoom: 6, maxNativeZoom: 8, maxZoom: 10, bounds: rasterBounds, noWrap: true },
      );
      nightDetail.on('tileerror', ({ tile }) => { tile.style.visibility = 'hidden'; });
      const roadsLayer = L.geoJSON(undefined, {
        style: { color: '#d5cfba', weight: 1.1, opacity: 0.55 }, interactive: false,
      });
      const parkBoundaries = L.geoJSON(undefined, {
        style: { color: '#86e1b6', weight: 1.5, opacity: 0.9, fillOpacity: 0, dashArray: '5 4' },
        onEachFeature(feature, layer) {
          if (feature.properties?.NAME) layer.bindPopup(feature.properties.NAME + ' National Park');
        },
      });
      fetch(container.dataset.roads!).then(response => response.json()).then(data => roadsLayer.addData(data));
      fetch(container.dataset.parks!).then(response => response.json()).then(data => parkBoundaries.addData(data));
      let satellite = false;
      function updateRelief() {
        reliefToggle.disabled = satellite;
        reliefStrength.disabled = satellite || !reliefToggle.checked;
        if (reliefToggle.checked && !satellite) terrainRelief.addTo(map);
        else terrainRelief.remove();
        sourceNote.textContent = satellite
          ? 'Satellite night lights · NASA Black Marble 2016'
          : reliefToggle.checked ? 'Modelled sky brightness · 2016 atlas + terrain relief at regional scale'
          : 'Modelled sky brightness · 2016 atlas';
      }
      reliefToggle.addEventListener('change', updateRelief);
      reliefStrength.addEventListener('input', () => {
        const strength = Number(reliefStrength.value);
        reliefValue.value = strength + '%';
        terrainRelief.setOpacity(strength * 0.0076);
      });
      modeButtons.forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const nextSatellite = button.dataset.mode === 'satellite';
        if (nextSatellite === satellite) return;
        satellite = nextSatellite;
        if (satellite) {
          map.setMaxZoom(10);
          map.removeLayer(skyAtlas);
          satelliteOverview.addTo(map);
          nightDetail.addTo(map);
        } else {
          map.setMaxZoom(8);
          map.removeLayer(nightDetail);
          map.removeLayer(satelliteOverview);
          skyAtlas.addTo(map);
        }
        modeButtons.forEach(option => option.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String((option.dataset.mode === 'satellite') === satellite)));
        updateRelief();
      }));

      function placeLayer(places: Place[], kind: string, radius: number, color: string) {
        return L.layerGroup(places.map(([name, lat, lng]) => L.circleMarker([lat, lng], {
          radius, color, weight: 1.5, fillOpacity: 0.85, interactive: false,
        }).bindTooltip(name, {
          permanent: true, direction: 'right', offset: [radius + 2, 0],
          className: 'place-label ' + kind,
        })));
      }

      placeLayer(capitals, 'capital-label', 4, '#ffe3ac').addTo(map);
      const regionalLayer = placeLayer(centres, 'regional-label', 3, '#a8cde4');
      const parkLayer = placeLayer(parks, 'park-label', 4, '#87dfb6');
      function updateLabels() {
        const zoom = map.getZoom();
        if (zoom >= 6 && roadsToggle.checked) roadsLayer.addTo(map); else roadsLayer.remove();
        if (zoom >= 6.5 && parksToggle.checked) parkBoundaries.addTo(map); else parkBoundaries.remove();
        if (zoom >= 5) regionalLayer.addTo(map); else regionalLayer.remove();
        if (zoom >= 6.5) parkLayer.addTo(map); else parkLayer.remove();
        status.textContent = zoom >= 6.5
          ? 'Local view · selected national parks visible'
          : zoom >= 5 ? 'Regional view · zoom in for national parks'
          : 'National view · zoom in for regional centres';
      }
      map.on('zoomend', updateLabels);
      roadsToggle.addEventListener('change', updateLabels);
      parksToggle.addEventListener('change', updateLabels);
      updateLabels();
    </script>
    <style>
      :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
      :global(body) { margin: 0; background: #101719; color: #f0eadd; font: 1rem/1.6 Arial, sans-serif; }
      main { max-width: 1440px; margin: auto; padding: 0 5vw 64px; }
      header { padding: 20px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #45504d; }
      a { color: #edc08e; }
      .intro { margin: 36px 0 28px; }
      .intro p, .notes p { max-width: 740px; color: #c6cfcb; }
      .eyebrow { color: #d6a66c; font-size: .875rem; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: .14em; }
      h1 { font: 400 clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 6.5rem)/1 Georgia, serif; margin: 14px 0; }
      h2 { font: 400 2rem Georgia, serif; }
      .map-panel { border: 1px solid #45504d; background: #182326; }
      .toolbar { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; padding: 12px 16px; }
      .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 20px; font-size: .875rem; }
      .map-actions { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .subtitle { color: #83d7df !important; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 4px 0; }
      .legend i { display: inline-block; width: .55rem; height: .55rem; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 5px; }
      .city { background: #ffe3ac; } .town { background: #a8cde4; } .park { background: #87dfb6; }
      .legend .park-boundary, .legend .road { width: .85rem; height: 0; border-radius: 0; vertical-align: middle; }
      .legend .park-boundary { border-top: 2px dashed #86e1b6; }
      .legend .road { border-top: 1px solid #d5cfba; }
      button { font: inherit; background: #25383c; color: #f0eadd; border: 1px solid #688181; border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 12px; cursor: pointer; }
      #night-map { height: clamp(400px, 67vh, 760px); background: #04050e; isolation: isolate; position: relative; }
      .fallback { position: absolute; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; pointer-events: none; }
      .has-map .fallback { display: none; }
      .caption { margin: 0; padding: 8px 16px; color: #c6cfcb; font-size: .875rem; }
      .sky-key { padding: 12px 16px 18px; font-size: .8rem; }
      .swatches { display: flex; height: 14px; margin-top: 8px; border: 1px solid #55606b; }
      .swatches i { flex: 1; }
      .swatches i:nth-child(1) { background: #050505; } .swatches i:nth-child(2) { background: #74747e; } .swatches i:nth-child(3) { background: #173f96; } .swatches i:nth-child(4) { background: #00a66f; } .swatches i:nth-child(5) { background: #ebdc05; } .swatches i:nth-child(6) { background: #f12d20; } .swatches i:nth-child(7) { background: #e58bd3; }
      .key-ends { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
      .notes { margin-top: 40px; }
      #night-map :global(.place-label) {
        color: #ffe3ac; background: #0b101a; border: 0; box-shadow: none;
        border-radius: 3px; padding: 1px 4px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;
      }
      #night-map :global(.place-label::before) { display: none; }
      #night-map :global(.regional-label) { color: #a8cde4; }
      #night-map :global(.park-label) { color: #87dfb6; }
      .guide, .nearby { margin: 44px 0 28px; }
      .section-heading { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
      .section-heading h2 { margin: 5px 0 0; }
      .section-heading > p { max-width: 420px; margin: 0; color: #adbab8; }
      .stop-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 10px; }
      .stop { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: start; min-height: 118px; padding: 16px 18px; text-align: left; background: #172225; border: 1px solid #344b4d; transition: background .2s, border-color .2s, transform .2s; }
      .stop:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); background: #203237; border-color: #87dfb6; }
      .stop[aria-pressed="true"] { background: linear-gradient(125deg, #24454a, #172225 80%); border-color: #83d7df; box-shadow: inset 3px 0 #83d7df; }
      .stop small, .travel-time { color: #86d4d6; font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .12em; font-weight: 700; }
      .stop strong { font: 400 1.25rem/1.25 Georgia, serif; margin-top: 7px; }
      .stop span { color: #a9b9b6; font-size: .85rem; margin-top: auto; }
      .layer-options { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 7px 16px 10px; border-top: 1px solid #344548; font-size: .82rem; }
      .layer-options > span:first-child { color: #8ea6a4; font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .11em; }
      .layer-options label { cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; }
      .layer-options label:has(input:disabled) { opacity: .5; cursor: not-allowed; }
      .layer-options input { accent-color: #83d7df; vertical-align: middle; }
      .relief-strength { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
      .relief-strength input { width: 88px; cursor: pointer; }
      .relief-strength output { min-width: 2.6em; text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
      .map-hint { margin-left: auto; color: #9bb1ae; }
      .mode-switch { display: flex; border: 1px solid #688181; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
      .mode-switch button { border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: transparent; padding: 6px 10px; }
      .mode-switch button + button { border-left: 1px solid #688181; }
      .mode-switch button[aria-pressed="true"] { background: #83d7df; color: #0b1b20; font-weight: 700; }
      .map-caption { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px; align-items: center; }
      .source-note { margin: 0; padding: 8px 16px; font-size: .78rem; color: #a0b7b2; }
      .view-note { margin-top: 14px; padding: 22px 28px; border: 1px solid #426069; background: linear-gradient(110deg, #173036, #172124 75%); }
      .view-note .eyebrow { margin: 0; color: #83d7df; }
      .view-note h2 { margin: 4px 0 6px; }
      .view-note > p:last-child { margin: 0; color: #c5d1ce; max-width: 850px; }
      .nearby { margin-top: 66px; }
      .near-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 12px; }
      .near-grid article { padding: 24px; background: #192629; border: 1px solid #3d5556; display: flex; align-items: start; flex-direction: column; }
      .near-grid h3 { font: 400 1.75rem/1.2 Georgia, serif; margin: 10px 0; }
      .near-grid p { color: #c1cdca; margin: 0 0 16px; }
